Interview Questions
1. What is Bias?

Bias is the error caused by an overly simple model that fails to capture the underlying pattern, leading to underfitting.

2. What is Variance?

Variance is the error caused by a model being too sensitive to the training data, leading to overfitting.

3. Difference between Bias and Variance?
Bias	Variance
Too Simple	Too Complex
Underfitting	Overfitting
High Train Error	Low Train Error
High Test Error	High Test Error
4. What is Underfitting?

When a model is too simple to learn the underlying relationship in the data.

5. What is Overfitting?

When a model learns both the true patterns and the random noise in the training data, resulting in poor performance on unseen data.

6. What is the Bias-Variance Tradeoff?

The process of balancing model simplicity (bias) and model complexity (variance) to achieve the best generalization on unseen data.

7. How do Ridge and Lasso help?

They reduce overfitting by penalizing large coefficients, thereby lowering variance.
